### VS Code REST Client (extension humao.rest-client). Start the server first: npm run dev
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check -> 200
GET {{base}}/health

### Register -> 201
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

### Duplicate email -> 409
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "Alice@Example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

### Weak password -> 400 with details
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "password": "short" }

### Login -> 200 { token }; the token is stored in a variable for the requests below
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse 42" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Wrong password -> 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "wrong password" }

### Current user -> 200
GET {{base}}/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{base}}/profile

### Create a diagram, the owner is the caller -> 201
POST {{base}}/diagrams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "title": "Login flow", "notation": "UML", "sourceCode": "user -> server", "priority": "low" }

### Partial update of my diagram -> 200 (only the sent fields change; replace 1 with an id of yours)
PATCH {{base}}/diagrams/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "priority": "high" }

### Empty PATCH body -> 400
PATCH {{base}}/diagrams/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{}

### List diagrams -> 200
GET {{base}}/diagrams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Somebody else's diagram -> 403 (replace 1 with an id owned by another user)
DELETE {{base}}/diagrams/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin only: regular user -> 403
GET {{base}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Page 2 of size 5, sorted by title descending -> 200 (X-Total-Count has the full size)
GET {{base}}/diagrams?limit=5&offset=5&sort=title&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Page size over 100 -> 400
GET {{base}}/diagrams?limit=1000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unknown sort field -> 400
GET {{base}}/diagrams?sort=password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Advanced authentication (refresh, 2FA, password reset, roles, audit) ---
### Login returns accessToken and refreshToken; the refresh token is kept for the next requests
# @name login2
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "correct horse 42", "deviceName": "REST Client" }

###
@refresh = {{login2.response.body.refreshToken}}

### Exchange the refresh token -> 200 (a new pair; the old refresh token stops working, reusing it revokes the session)
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### Own sessions -> 200
GET {{base}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### End one session -> 204 (404 for an id that is not yours)
DELETE {{base}}/auth/sessions/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log out with the refresh token -> 204
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### End all sessions -> 204
POST {{base}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change the password -> 204 (other sessions end)
POST {{base}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "currentPassword": "correct horse 42", "newPassword": "another horse 43" }

### Ask for a reset -> 202 (the token is written to the server console, never to the response)
POST {{base}}/auth/password-reset/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com" }

### Confirm the reset with the token from the console -> 204
POST {{base}}/auth/password-reset/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste-the-token-here", "newPassword": "a brand new horse 44" }

### Two-factor state -> 200
GET {{base}}/auth/2fa
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Start two-factor setup -> 201 { secret, otpauthUrl }
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/setup
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "password": "correct horse 42" }

### Enable it with a code from the authenticator -> 200 { recoveryCodes }
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "code": "123456" }

### Second step of a login with 2FA -> 200 (challengeToken comes from the login answer)
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeToken": "paste-the-challenge-here", "code": "123456" }

### Disable two-factor -> 204
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "password": "correct horse 42", "code": "123456" }

### Admin: audit trail -> 200 (needs the audit:read permission)
GET {{base}}/admin/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: roles and permissions -> 200
GET {{base}}/admin/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{base}}/admin/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: create a role from permissions you hold -> 201 (403 for a permission you lack)
POST {{base}}/admin/roles
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "name": "reviewer", "description": "Reads diagrams", "permissions": ["diagram:read", "profile:read"] }

### Admin: assign a role -> 200 (the last administrator cannot be demoted)
PATCH {{base}}/users/2/role
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "role": "moderator" }

### Admin: unlock an account -> 200
POST {{base}}/users/2/unlock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
